      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        830,
        464
      ],
      "notes": "Fixes the documented 'if the item wasn't found, this will error -- acceptable for v1' gap on Delete Row: an unhandled error here used to block the whole webhook response (same failure class as the Check Budget Alert outage from earlier tonight), taking the entire app offline on a single failed remove instead of just no-op'ing that one action. False branch skips straight to Get Current List/Get Settings so the webhook still returns a valid, unchanged list. Left value uses `|| \"\"` because the alwaysOutputData placeholder has no row_number key at all (JS undefined), and undefined !== \"\" would otherwise be true. Wrapped in String(...) because Google Sheets returns row_number as a real number, and this node's strict type validation throws on comparing a number against a string operator rather than silently coercing it (found live 2026-08-08, right after the underlying Find Row to Remove filter itself got fixed)."
    },
